      <div type="clause" n="El. 41">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> El. 41</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 41" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="40" ed="#liebermann"/>Ne wend<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.15"/> ðu ðe no<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.12"/> on þæs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.16"/> folces unræd ⁊ unryht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.17"/> gewill on hiora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.18"/> spræce ⁊ geclysp<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.19"/> ofer ðin<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.20"/> ryht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.21"/>, ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.22"/> ðæs unwisestan lare ne him ne geðafa.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 41" corresp="#wit-g-prol-only"><pb n="40" ed="#liebermann"/>Ne wend þu ðe ná on ðæs folces únræd ⁊ unriht gewill on hyra spæce ⁊ geclæsp ofer ðin riht, ⁊ on þæs unwisestan lare ne him ne geðafa.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 41" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="41" ed="#liebermann"/>Ne gewend<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.5"/> þu ðe no<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.2"/> on þæs folces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.6"/> unræd, ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.2"/> on unriht gewil<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.7"/> on hiora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.8"/> spræce ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.2"/> geclebs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.9"/> ofer ðin ryht, ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.2"/> þæs unwisestan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.10"/> lare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.11"/> þu ne geþafa.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="El. 41" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="41" ed="#liebermann"/>Non sequeris turbam ad faciendum malum nec in iudicio plurimorum adquiesces sententiæ, ut a uero deuies. Pauperis quoque non misereberis in iudicio.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.7-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="MP 41" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="258" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Ne wend ðu ðe no on þæs folces unræd ⁊ unryht gewill on hiora spræce ⁊ geclysp ofer ðin ryht, ⁊ ðæs unwisestan lare ne him ne geðafa.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="41" ed="#liebermann"/>Richte du<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.1"/> dich nicht nach der Menge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.2"/> Unverstand<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.3"/> und unrechtem Begehr gemäss ihrem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.4"/> Verhandeln<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.5"/> und Geschrei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.6"/> wider dein richtiges [Gefühl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.7"/>]; und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.8"/> die Lehre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.9"/> des Thörichtsten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.10"/> gieb<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.11"/> ihnen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.12"/> nicht zu.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.13"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Do not follow the folly and wrongful desire of the crowd according to their talk and clamour against your right [sense]; and do not concede the teaching of the most foolish to them.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="409" ed="#whitelock"/>Do not thou turn thyself to the folly and unjust will of the people in their speech and clamour, against thy right [judgment], and do not yield for them to the teaching of the most foolish.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="259" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Do not turn to the folly and unjust desire of the people, in their words and their clamor, against that which is lawful for you, nor agree to their most unwise counsel.</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">Exodus 23,2</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="41">Exodus 23.2</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">[23, 2]</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wende <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wende So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">na <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">na So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ungeriht wille <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ungeriht wille So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">heora <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">heora So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gecleps <hi rend="italic">So Ld; über</hi> p <hi rend="italic">steht</hi> f <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gecleps So Ld; f written above p So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þine <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þine So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">riht <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">riht So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">on <hi rend="italic">fügt zu So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">on added by So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">41</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ge <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ge written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">41</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geändert in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">41</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ol <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ol on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">41</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> gewillon h.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to gewillon h.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">41</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">41</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ebs <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ebs on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">41</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">un <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">un written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">41</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt Rasur von sechs Buchst.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by an erasure of six letters</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">41</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nec declinabis in iudicio pauperis (<hi rend="italic">s. u. El.</hi> 43) <hi rend="italic">fügt hier zu Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nec declinabis in iudicio pauperis (see below El. 43) added here by Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Kehre, wende’. — Zwar lässt Af <hi rend="italic">in iudicio</hi> hier fort, aber wohl nur, weil er den Satz als Fortsetzung von 40 nimmt. Offenbar zeigt seine wortreichere Bearbeitung hier und 43, wie praktisch er diese biblische Warnung zur Gerechtigkeit (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl.</hi> 2d) hielt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Turn, direct’. — Af does, it is true, leave out <hi rend="italic">in iudicio</hi> here, but probably only because he takes the sentence as a continuation of 40. His wordier adaptation here and in 43 evidently shows how practical he considered this biblical warning to justice (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl.</hi> 2d)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Volk’ hier = Pöbel</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘People’ here = the rabble</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘üblem Rat’, doch auch ‘imprudentia’; Grein. Die Erklärer interpungieren verschieden, Toller wie ich, Turk schon hier. Er macht also <hi rend="italic">gewill, geclysp, lare</hi> zu Objekten von <hi rend="italic">geþafa.</hi> Allein <hi rend="italic">unræd</hi> und <hi rend="italic">unriht</hi> scheint mir alliterierend zu Einem Satzglied gehörig; auch pflegt Ælfred eine längere Reihe von Objekten, denen das Verb folgt, durch ein Demonstrativ aufzunehmen. Schmid interpungiert hinter <hi rend="italic">gewill,</hi> so dass zweites <hi rend="italic">on</hi> das erste wiederholt. Da fiele die Auslassung von ‘und’ auf. — Price-Thorpe übersetzt das zweite <hi rend="italic">on</hi>: ‘in’, was zu <hi rend="italic">geclysp</hi> nicht passt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘evil counsel’, but also ‘imprudentia’; Grein. The commentators punctuate differently, Toller as I do, Turk already here. He thus makes <hi rend="italic">gewill, geclysp, lare</hi> objects of <hi rend="italic">geþafa.</hi> But <hi rend="italic">unræd</hi> and <hi rend="italic">unriht</hi>, alliterating, seem to me to belong to a single member of the sentence; and Ælfred is also accustomed to take up a longer series of objects followed by the verb with a demonstrative. Schmid punctuates after <hi rend="italic">gewill,</hi> so that the second <hi rend="italic">on</hi> repeats the first. The omission of ‘and’ would then be striking. — Price-Thorpe translates the second <hi rend="italic">on</hi> ‘in’, which does not suit <hi rend="italic">geclysp</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Pluralisch wird <hi rend="italic">folc</hi> öfter konstruiert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">folc</hi> is often construed as a plural</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Rede’ Schmid, ‘speech’ Price-Thorpe, aus Zusammenhang ungünstigen Nebensinn ‘Geschwätz’ vermuten lassend. Vielleicht aber im Sinne von ‘beratende Versammlung eines Kollegiums’; für <hi rend="italic">colloquium, consilium, disputatio</hi> Toller, auch mittelengl. für ‘meeting’; dies käme <hi rend="italic">iudicio</hi> der Vulg. nahe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘talk’ Schmid, ‘speech’ Price-Thorpe, which from the context suggests an unfavourable secondary sense, ‘chatter’. But perhaps in the sense of ‘deliberative assembly of a body’; for <hi rend="italic">colloquium, consilium, disputatio</hi> Toller, also in Middle English for ‘meeting’; this would come close to <hi rend="italic">iudicio</hi> of the Vulg.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Von <hi rend="italic">clipian</hi> lärmen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">From <hi rend="italic">clipian</hi>, to make a noise</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘über dein Recht’ Schmid, allein Vulg. spricht nicht von egoistischem Anspruchverfolgen, sondern vom Verharren bei ‘Wahrheit, Billigkeit, Pflicht’ — alles Bed. von <hi rend="italic">riht; s. Wb</hi> 3. Richtig ‘against thine own reason’ Price-Thorpe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘beyond your right’ Schmid; but the Vulg. speaks not of selfishly pursuing a claim but of holding fast to ‘truth, equity, duty’ — all meanings of <hi rend="italic">riht; see Wb</hi> 3. Correctly ‘against thine own reason’ Price-Thorpe</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Einfügung <hi rend="italic">on</hi> (G. So. Ld, auch Schmid) scheint nicht authentisch; <hi rend="italic">geþafian on</hi> ist nicht belegt; der Zufüger liess es vielleicht noch vom vorherigen <hi rend="italic">wend</hi> abhängen und interpungierte mit Price-Thorpe hinter <hi rend="italic">lare.</hi> Price-Thorpe übersetzt <hi rend="italic">on:</hi> ‘gemäss’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The insertion of <hi rend="italic">on</hi> (G. So. Ld, also Schmid) does not seem authentic; <hi rend="italic">geþafian on</hi> is not attested; the interpolator perhaps still made it depend on the preceding <hi rend="italic">wend</hi> and punctuated, with Price-Thorpe, after <hi rend="italic">lare.</hi> Price-Thorpe translates <hi rend="italic">on:</hi> ‘according to’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.9" n="9" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Oder ‘Lehren’ = Rat, Anregung</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Or ‘teachings’ = counsel, prompting</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.10" n="10" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Unwissendsten’ Schmid, allein Af negiert Weisheit, nicht Wissen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘most ignorant’ Schmid, but Af negates wisdom, not knowledge</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.11" n="11" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Price-Thorpe versteht ‘neither allow thou of them’ wohl meinend ‘stimme jenen [Torheiten] nicht bei’. Dies Personale für eine Reihe von Abstrakten scheint mir unmöglich. Zum Objektsaccus. <hi rend="italic">vgl. o.</hi> 40 <hi rend="italic">domas geþafa;</hi> zum Dativ <hi rend="italic">vgl.: þinum mæge man ne geþafa</hi> in <hi rend="italic">Fæder lar</hi> 18</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Price-Thorpe understands ‘neither allow thou of them’, probably meaning ‘do not assent to those [follies]’. This personal pronoun for a series of abstracts seems to me impossible. For the object accus. <hi rend="italic">cf. above</hi> 40 <hi rend="italic">domas geþafa;</hi> for the dative <hi rend="italic">cf.: þinum mæge man ne geþafa</hi> in <hi rend="italic">Fæder lar</hi> 18</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.12" n="12" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘der Menge’, oder ‘ihm’, dem Toren</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘the multitude’, or ‘him’, the fool</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-41.lnote.de.13" n="13" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die hier in der Exodus 23, 3 folgende Mahnung, zugunsten Armer nicht das Recht zu beugen, fehlt; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> arm 6c. Af verbindet den Satz mit 23, 6 zu El 43; Quadr spät. Rez. schliesst 23, 6 hier an</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The exhortation that follows here in Exodus 23, 3, not to bend the law in favour of the poor, is lacking; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> arm 6c. Af combines the sentence with 23, 6 to form El 43; Quadr later rec. attaches 23, 6 here</seg></note>
      </div>
